<title>USA: Genelabs completes Phase 3 trials of GL701.</title>
<headline>Genelabs completes Phase 3 trials of GL701.</headline>
<dateline>REDWOOD CITY, Calif. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Genelabs Technologies Inc said it completed its first Phase III clinical trial of its lead compound GL701, being studied for the treatment of systemic lupus erythematosus.</p>
<p>It said it expects to report trials results in the first or second quarter of this year.</p>
<p>GL701, Genelabs' lead compound is a pharmaceutical formulation containing the active ingredient dehydroepiandrosterone, or DHEA, a naturally occurring hormone which is produced by the adrenal glands. Lupus patients generally have abnormally low levels of DHEA.</p>
</text>
